d 'POLYSEM': module to perform confirmatory factor analysis of ordinal indicators by diagonally weighted least squares on polychoric correlations
d
d      polysem fits the factor model R = Lambda Phi Lambda' + Theta
d to the polychoric, polyserial and Pearson correlations of the   
d indicators. Here Theta is diagonal with Theta_ii = 1 - (Lambda
d Phi Lambda')_ii, because the latent responses have unit variance.
d    The command:	 1. runs polycorr to obtain the vector of
d correlations r and its covariance matrix V;	     2. minimizes
d (r - sigma(theta))' W (r - sigma(theta)) by Gauss-Newton with
d step halving. 
d
d KW: confirmatory factor analysis
d KW: polychoric correlations
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 and polycorr from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author:  Yusuf Toyin Yusuf,  Kwara State University
d Support: email  YUSUF.YUSUF@@KWASU.EDU.NG
d
f polysem.ado
f polysem.sthlp
f polysem_examples.do
f polysem_cert.do
